00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.019 align:start position:0%
October 26th is Judgment Day for  Europe's banks the first stress tests of  the financial system in three years will  reveal once and for all which lenders  are equipped to survive an economic  shock if it works credit should start  flowing again and Europe will be jolted  out of its slump the last round of tests  in the aftermath of the sovereign debt  crisis wasn't stressful enough and the  results were incredible  this time 130 banks are under the  microscope in a two-part process run by  the European Central Bank and the  European Banking Authority the first is  a review of asset quality that'll  determine which banks have too many bad  loans the second is the actual stress  test which simulates crisis conditions  to gauge the resilience of bank balance  sheets ideally some banks will fail  otherwise the whole exercise won't  inspire confidence some of the most  vulnerable lenders are in Greece Austria  Italy and Portugal the bigger question  is how financial giants like Deutsche  Bank Barclays and BNP Paribas do any  institution falling short we'll have two  weeks to submit a capital plan and just  six to nine months to complete it
 

